sanas.com/","wd":"Q15260365","ds":"The Museum of Ancient Greek Technology \"Kostas Kotsanas\" is a private museum focused on ancient Greek technology and other cultural achievements of ancient Greece. It has four permanent annexes in Athens, Ancient Olympia, Katakolo and Heraklion and it is famous for its travelling exhibitions, domestically and abroad. In 2019 it has been nominated as “European Museum of the Year” by the European Museum Forum.","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Kotsanas_Museum_Athens.jpg/960px-Kotsanas_Museum_Athens.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","wpu":"Museum of Ancient Greek Technology"},{"n":"Katakolon","g":"sights","k":"viewpoint","la":37.649351,"lo":21.31449,"d":685},{"n":"Katakolon","g":"sights","k":"viewpoint","la":37.66022,"lo":21.314654,"d":1756},{"n":"Αρχαία Φειά","g":"sights","k":"archaeological_site","la":37.663727,"lo":21.314132,"d":2145,"wd":"Q3563531"},{"n":"Agios Andreas","g":"sights","k":"ruins","la":37.664043,"lo":21.314077,"d":2180},{"n":"Pontikokastro","g":"sights","k":"castle","la":37.664298,"lo":21.31402,"d":2209,"wd":"Q19826720","ds":"Pontikokastro (Greek: Ποντικόκαστρο), known in French as Beauvoir and Italian as Belveder during the late Middle Ages, is a Byzantine castle in Agios Andreas, Katakolo, in the Peloponnese peninsula of Greece.","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/34/Pontikokastro_%28Beauvoir%29_Castle.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","wpu":"Pontikokastro"},{"n":"Epihotel Odysseas","g":"sights","k":"hotel","la":37.664176,"lo":21.32764,"d":2235,"w":"https://hotelodysseas.gr/en/the-hotel/","ph":"+30 26210 41162","wifi":1},{"n":"PHEIA | West Peloponnese","g":"sights","k":"hotel","la":37.664143,"lo":21.310851,"d":2275,"w":"https://www.pheia.gr/","ph":"+30 26210 41 401","ad":"1 Agios Andreas","f":["wc","card"],"wifi":1},{"n":"Agios Andreas","g":"sights","k":"beach","la":37.664992,"l